      "worked": "Treat the equation as a quadratic in $e^x$:\n$$\\begin{align*}(e^x)^2-5e^x+4&=0\\\\(e^x-1)(e^x-4)&=0\\\\e^x&=1\\text{ or }e^x=4\\\\x&=\\ln 1\\text{ or }x=\\ln 4\\\\x&=0\\text{ or }x=\\ln 4\\end{align*}$$\nBoth exponential values are positive, so both solutions are valid.",
